# Android: bare workflow per Plan 07-03 fix (2026-05-24). Originally hybrid
# (3 customized files committed, rest auto-generated by `expo prebuild` on EAS
# Cloud), but EAS Cloud does NOT re-run prebuild when `android/` already exists
# — it tries to invoke `./gradlew` directly. Partial state caused `ENOENT:
# gradlew` on EAS Cloud build 9e243e59. Switched to committed-android: gradlew
# + wrapper + manifests + source + resources all in git; only true build
# outputs + machine-specific files remain ignored. On Expo SDK upgrades:
# re-run `expo prebuild --clean` and commit the diff.
/android/.gradle/
/android/build/
/android/captures/
/android/local.properties
/android/app/build/
/android/app/release/
/android/app/.cxx/
# debug.keystore: tracked in git (standard Android debug keystore, password
# 'android' is public knowledge per android.com docs). Same cert SHA-256
# across local + CI ensures Mapbox dev-token works in android-debug-apk.yml
# artifact. Was auto-gitignored by `npx expo prebuild`; we override that.
# release.keystore: prod signing keystore lives in SOPS at
# .secrets/prod/mobile-signing.yaml; the CI workflow writes it ephemerally at
# build time. Never commit. (Belt-and-suspenders: root .gitignore also has
# /apps/mobile-rn/android/app/release.keystore.)
/android/app/release.keystore
# Auto-generated /android/.gitignore from `expo prebuild` (duplicates ours).
/android/.gitignore
